    "narrative": "Ghost Ride the WHIP enters today\u2019s slate focusing on high-ceiling leadoff and high-order opportunities to capitalize on our SB-heavy identity. Our strongest play is **Corbin Carroll** (78.62), who benefits from a favorable draw against Mitch Keller; the synergy between his elite sprint speed and the projected order advantage makes him the anchor of our lineup. Closely trailing him is **James Wood** (76.28), whose 10% boost from the leadoff spot and a strong xwOBA against Woods Richardson solidify his status as an elite start. **Mickey Moniak** also earns a massive 75.98 rating, fueled by a high park factor and a significant platoon advantage against Christian Scott, making him an essential component of today\u2019s offensive output.\n\nThe most difficult roster decision involved our catcher tandem and the bottom of the order. While **Gabriel Moreno** (56.09) and **Luis Campusano** (52.71) remain in the lineup, they are essentially serving as placeholders; their sub-60 scores suggest they were the closest to being pushed aside for higher-upside bench options had they been active. Despite a robust 72.92 projection for **Vinnie Pasquantino**, he remains our most effective high-floor play against Cecconi. We are keeping a close watch on **Trevor Story**, whose score of 52.39 is tempered by the talent of Griffin Jax; we are specifically banking on the \"slow delivery\" window to exploit a stolen base opportunity, even if the matchup against Jax limits his overall ceiling.\n\nRisk management remains a priority given the volatility of \"Lineup Pending\" designations for **Gabriel Moreno**, **Luis Campusano**, **Trevor Story**, **Tyler Soderstrom**, and **Corbin Carroll**. Should official lineups move these players down in the order, their efficiency scores will drop immediately, potentially triggering benching decisions. Our bench depth\u2014including **Jose Caballero**, **Josh Naylor**, **Brice Turang**, and **Seiya Suzuki**\u2014is currently neutralized by off-days or rest, but we are keeping our eyes on **Austin Riley**, **Giancarlo Stanton**, **Max Muncy**, **Carson Williams**, **Zach McKinstry**, **Dalton Rushing**, **Alex Freeland**, and **Cole Young** for potential late-game pivots or future rotation needs as the season progresses.",
